,"also":"","summary":"The pining one, the younger son of Elimelech and Naomi, and husband of Orpah, Ruth’s sister (Ruth 1:2; 4:9).","verses":3,"father":"Elimelech","mother":"Naomi","v":[9]},{"id":"rachel_2386","name":"Rachel","also":"Rahel","summary":"Ewe, “the daughter”, “the somewhat petulant, peevish, and self-willed though beautiful younger daughter” of Laban, and one of Jacob’s wives (Gen. 29:6, 28).","verses":45,"father":"Laban","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"leah_1813","name":"Leah","also":"","summary":"Weary, the eldest daughter of Laban, and sister of Rachel (Gen. 29:16). Jacob took her to wife through a deceit of her father (Gen. 29:23). She was “tender-eyed” (17).","verses":32,"father":"Laban","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"judah_1751","name":"Judah","also":"","summary":"Praise, the fourth son of Jacob by Leah.","verses":245,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[12]},{"id":"pharez_2338","name":"Pharez","also":"Phares, Perez","summary":"Pharez,, breach, the son of Judah (Neh. 11:4). “The chief of all the captains of the host for the first month” in the reign of David was taken from his family (1 Chr. 27:3).","verses":15,"father":"Judah","mother":"Tamar","v":[12,18]},{"id":"tamar_2821","name":"Tamar","also":"Thamar","summary":"The daughter-in-law of Judah, to whose eldest son, Er, she was married (Gen. 38:6). After her husband’s death, she was married to Onan, his brother (8), and on his death, Judah promised to her that his third son, Shelah, would become her husband.","verses":7,"father":"","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[17,22]},{"id":"jesse_903","name":"Jesse","also":"","summary":"Firm, or a gift, a son of Obed, the son of Boaz and Ruth (Ruth 4:17, 22; Matt. 1:5, 6; Luke 3:32). He was the father of eight sons, the youngest of whom was David (1 Sam. 17:12).","verses":44,"father":"Obed","mother":"","v":[17,22]},{"id":"obed_2228","name":"Obed","also":"","summary":"A son of Boaz and Ruth (Ruth 4:21, 22), and the grandfather of David (Matt. 1:5).","verses":6,"father":"Boaz","mother":"Ruth","v":[17,21,22]},{"id":"hezron_1520","name":"Hezron","also":"Esrom","summary":"The older of the two sons of Pharez (Gen. 46:12).","verses":13,"father":"Pharez","mother":"","v":[18,19]},{"id":"amminadab_228","name":"Amminadab","also":"Aminadab","summary":"The father of Nahshon, who was chief of the tribe of Judah (Num. 1:7; 2:3; 7:12, 17; 10:14).","verses":11,"father":"Ram","mother":"","v":[19,20]},{"id":"ram_2391","name":"Ram","also":"Aram","summary":"The son of Hezron, and one of the ancestors of the royal line (Ruth 4:19).","verses":6,"father":"Hezron","mother":"","v":[19]},{"id":"nahshon_2144","name":"Nahshon","also":"Naasson, Naashon","summary":"Sorcerer, the son of Aminadab, and prince of the children of Judah at the time of the first numbering of the tribes in the wilderness (Ex. 6:23).","verses":11,"father":"Amminadab","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"salmon_2463","name":"Salmon","also":"Salma","summary":"Shady; or Zalmon, a hill covered with dark forests, south of Shechem, from which Abimelech and his men gathered wood to burn that city (Judg. 9:48).","verses":6,"father":"Nahshon","mother":"","v":[20,21]}],"places":[{"id":"moab_815","name":"Moab","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.49916,"lon":35.78051,"summary":"The land of Moab (Jer. 48:24), called also the “country of Moab” (Ruth 1:2, 6; 2:6), on the east of Jordan and the Dead Sea, and south of the Arnon (Num. 21:13, 26).","verses":148,"v":[3]},{"id":"bethlehem_218","name":"Bethlehem","kind":"City","lat":31.70431,"lon":35.20746,"summary":"A city in the “hill country” of Judah. It was originally called Ephrath (Gen. 35:16, 19; 48:7; Ruth 4:11). It was also called Beth-lehem Ephratah (Micah 5:2), Beth-lehem-judah (1 Sam. 17:12), and “the city of David” (Luke 2:4).","verses":32,"v":[11]},{"id":"ephrathah_404","name":"Ephrathah","kind":"","lat":31.70536,"lon":35.21027,"summary":"The ancient name of Bethlehem in Judah (Gen. 35:16, 19; 48:7). In Ruth 1:2 it is called “Bethlehem-Judah,” but the inhabitants are called “Ephrathites;” in Micah 5:2, “Bethlehem-Ephratah;” in Matt. 2:6, “Bethlehem in the land of Judah.”","verses":2,"v":[11]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1162,1162,5927,8179,8179,8179,3427,3427,3427,8033,2009,1350,1350,1162,1162,1162,1696,1696,5674,5674,559,559,559,5493,5493,6311,6423,6423,3427,3427,3427,5493,5493,5493,5493,3427,3427,3427],[3947,3947,3947,6235,2205,2205,2205,5892,5892,5892,559,559,3427,6311,3427,3427,3427,3427],[559,559,559,1350,1350,1350,5281,7725,7725,7725,7704,7704,7704,4124,4124,4376,4376,2513,2513,7704,7704,834,251,251,251,251,458],[589,559,1540,1540,1540,241,559,7069,7069,7069,7069,7069,5048,5048,5048,5048,3427,3427,3427,5048,5048,5048,5048,5048,2205,2205,5971,5971,5971,518,1350,1350,1350,1350,1350,1350,1350,518,518,518,3808,3808,1350,1350,5046,0,3045,3045,3045,3045,3588,369,369,369,369,2108,2108,1350,1350,1350,595,595,595,310,310,310,595,1350,1350,1350,559,559],[1162,1162,559,3117,3117,3117,7069,7069,7704,7704,3027,5281,854,854,854,7327,4125,4125,7069,7069,7069,7069,802,802,4191,4191,4191,6965,6965,6965,6965,8034,8034,8034,4191,4191,4191,5921,5159,5159],[1350,1350,559,3808,3808,1350,1350,0,6435,7843,7843,7843,5159,5159,5159,1353,1353,1353,1353,1353,3588,3808,3808,1350,1350],[2063,6440,6440,6440,3478,3478,5921,1353,1353,8545,8545,8545,8545,3605,3605,3605,1697,6965,6965,376,376,8025,8025,5275,5275,5414,5414,5414,7453,7453,7453,7453,2063,2063,2063,8584,8584,3478,3478],[1350,1350,1350,8025,5275,5275,559,559,1162,1162,7069,7069,0,0],[1162,1162,1162,559,2205,2205,2205,3605,3605,5971,5971,859,5707,5707,3117,3588,7069,7069,7069,3027,5281,3605,834,458,458,458,3630,4248,4248],[1571,7069,7069,7069,7327,4125,4125,4248,802,802,802,802